			},
			"date": "2023-02-16T21:48:28.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> the shadowroot attribute got deprecated in favor of shadowrootmode.</p><p>\"Summary<br>The standards-track `shadowrootmode` attribute, which enables declarative Shadow DOM, was shipped in Chrome 111. The older, non-standard `shadowroot` attribute is now deprecated. During the deprecation period, both attributes are functional, however the `shadowroot` attribute does not enable the new streaming behavior, whereas `shadowrootmode` allows streaming of content. There is a straightforward migration path: replace `shadowroot` with `shadowrootmode`.\"</p><p><a href=\"https://botsin.space/@intenttoship/109843427498199155\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">botsin.space/@intenttoship/109</span><span class=\"invisible\">843427498199155</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109876648508373899",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@deebloo/109876648482115521",
			"author": {
				"name": "Danny Blue",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@deebloo",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/311/543/538/710/081/original/16eaa48f74ac1854.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-16T21:56:42.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> they changed the behavior to attach the shadow root after the opening tag so that streaming would work. Part of that change also changed the attribute name.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
